From c45b654f99d2c71e1247a06b661fcda248d84884 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ms178 <m.seyfarth@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:15:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 24/49] strided: four-lane exact gather, displaced streams,
 constant-multiply strength reduction on the #1035 plan structure

Ports this series' strided i32 reducer onto #1035's transactional
skeleton (VectorSchedule / PreheaderPlan / IvPlan, refusal before
mutation, phi prevalidation, parallel preheader spans), replacing the
two-lane SSE2 X4/X4Compact forms:

* SSE2 X4 fills all four lanes: VecLoadStrided2I32x4 gathers four exact
  dwords (movd + punpckldq/punpcklqdq, never touching a gap); with the
  contiguous-object proof VecLoadStrided2CompactI32x4 compacts two full
  loads with one shufps. One layout, so proven and unproven streams mix
  and no lane mask exists. llvm-mca Alder Lake: 0.50 vs 0.84
  cycles/element; Callgrind sum_dynamic_tail 5,913 Ir (main 9,243,
  gcc-16 -O2 6,167).
* load() is total: the compact form is selected only with the proof, so
  the invalid combination is unrepresentable rather than a runtime None.
* Streams may carry a constant displacement ((Value, i64) load bases,
  checked_add, stream_disp_fits keeps it a 32-bit address displacement).
* MulPlan: multiplication by a constant becomes shift/add/sub when exact
  modulo 2^32; 0 and -1 return None (the generic pmulld path is exact).
* main's dead two-lane X4 even-lane mask in emit_reduce is removed (it
  would zero lanes 1 and 3 under the four-lane layout).
