From 5bed032568874d97d84fe779a8dcca7252ac52f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ms178 <m.seyfarth@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:09:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 27/49] x86-64: exact loop_memset model with trip guard, soft
 call-argument register preferences, scaled-index LEA fold

loop_memset (fill loops -> memset):
* Exact affine address model: the store address is base + scale*iv + disp
  with every term proven; extended start offsets (d + k + i) are folded
  only where the narrow i + k cannot wrap (matched signedness, no counter
  wrap), Ne exits use the modular count with zero-extension.
* Trip-count guard: the call is reached only when the loop would run
  at least once, so a zero-trip loop never calls memset with a wrapped
  length (loop_memset_trip_guard{,_Os}.c). Cast memo cleared per plan
  (take()).
* The guard block's operand computations live in
  emit_trip_and_call_operands (apply_idiom was over 500 lines);
  call operands are materialized in M (CallOperands).

Register allocation: a value passed to direct calls in one consistent
integer slot prefers that slot's register (collect_outgoing_arg_prefs).
Preferences are soft (RegAllocConfig::reg_prefs -> LiveRange::reg_pref):
reg_hints is the ParamRef ordered-copy contract (never evicted, never
exchanged), and putting outgoing slots there made argument values
unevictable (lz4: 25 -> 35 stack operands). Values with an incoming
parameter hint get no preference. Callgrind Ir vs preferences off:
loop_patterns -6.92%, sqlite_varint -1.67% (-Os),
zlib_ng_adler32_combine -1.61%, binary_trees -0.45% (-Os),
expat_siphash24 +0.081% (sole regression); outputs identical.
Preference-aware rotation was measured and rejected (gzip_longest_match
+1.64%, sqlite_varint +1.67%).

Peephole: shlq $s,%T (s = 1..3) feeding leaq (%B,%T),%D becomes
leaq (%B,%T,2^s),%D when %T dies there and the flags are dead. leaq
consumers only: memory consumers belong to fold_shift_into_sib
(check_rmw_sib_folds.sh contract 2c).
