Subject: [PATCH 33/49] ir: keep source spans parallel to instructions; verify
 it; fix every producer

`BasicBlock::source_spans` is either empty (untracked) or exactly parallel
to `instructions`; `.loc` emission and the phi copy placement read it by
index. ~18 passes and two lowering sites edited `instructions` alone, so a
span drifted onto the wrong instruction (wrong debug line) or ran short,
and phi_eliminate's `place_pred_copies` drained a short span vector and
panicked: the ICE behind 9 of the 86 benchmark programs at -O2 after the
previous commit (which this one fixes).

* `BasicBlock` edit primitives (`insert_inst(s)`, `push_inst`,
  `extend_insts`, `remove_inst(s)`, `retain_insts`, `clear_insts`,
  `replace_insts`, `span_at`, `append_spanned`): they keep a parallel
  block parallel and never panic on, repair, or start tracking a drifted
  one. Two whole-body operations normalise by contract:
  `replace_insts_synthesized` (consistent dummy spans) and
  `take_parallel_spans` (untracked). Synthesized instructions get dummy
  spans; replacements inherit the replaced span. No codegen decision may
  depend on span state.
* Verifier check 1a (`CCC_VERIFY_IR`): a tracked block whose span count
  differs from its instruction count is a violation (T6 aborts on it);
  `ir_verify_sweep.py` reports it as SPAN_DRIFT.
* Producers fixed: int/fp const hoists, range_check, vec_arx, fortify_fold,
  expr_sink (its span-dependent decision removed), vectorize, loop_rotate,
  arx_vectorize, reassoc_accum, aggregate_pair_roundtrip, outline_switch,
  copy_prop, loop_unroll, sccp, split_ranges, if_convert, bool_thread,
  const_array_promote, loop_idiom, loop_memset, the inliner's va_arg_pack
  filter, pgo + -finstrument-functions entry hooks (split_off/reappend ->
  insert_insts), nested functions (SetStaticChain splice carries its span,
  remove_entry_alloca via retain_insts), and phi copy placement rewritten
  on the primitives.

Evidence: drift 24/86 -> 0/86 programs (-O2); regression corpus
445/1220 -> 0 configs at -O2 on x86-64/i686/arm/riscv and at O0..Os on
x86-64. -O2 codegen is byte-identical on 85/86 programs
(zlib_ng_compare256: Callgrind 86,622,549 -> 86,622,615 Ir, neutral).
Tests: span_edit_tests (directed + a seeded random edit sequence checked
against a reference model with explicit tracking state), verify tests.
