From a93a1e5eff35f94ad791107bb7f146a0b5645fab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ms178 <m.seyfarth@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 13:27:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 35/49] loop_invert: bottom-test every unconditional latch, not
 only a sole one

`loop_invert` rotated a loop only when its header had exactly one latch.
`phi_relay_fold` folds a loop's shared relay latch into the header, so
every predecessor of the former relay becomes a latch -- and the multi-latch
loop then fell back to a top test: each back edge was a taken `jmp` to the
header's compare (the t1 `name_len` duplication and the expat scanners).

Each `Branch(H)` latch is now rotated on its own, one per round with every
guard re-derived on the new CFG: after the first rotation `H` still heads
the loop the remaining back edges close, and the copy argument is per edge
(the copied test runs at the end of its own latch, after that latch's phi
copies). Conditional latches keep their edge to `H`, which stays correct.
The induction-based follow-up folds (`fold_value_bound_after_invert`,
`downcount_after_invert`) still run only for a sole latch, which is now
tracked exactly.

Callgrind Ir (-O2): expat_xml_scan 1,491,021 -> 1,433,117 (-3.9 %),
expat_utf8_content 5,190,345 -> 4,969,575 (-4.3 %), linux_rbtree 485,993
-> 470,026 (-3.3 %), lz4_compress -0.14 %, t1 name_len 66,537,819 ->
62,765,019 (below main's 62,929,502). zstd_double_fast was +0.11 % from
an unrelated missed load fold the new register assignment exposed (fixed
in the next commit; with it, -0.25 %). Static: +49 instructions over the
86 programs (copied exit tests), outweighed dynamically everywhere
measured. Codegen-gate baseline: expat_xml_scan 195 -> 203 static.
