From e35632fabbe096e53a32b1ea61a56e12f7952c91 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ms178 <m.seyfarth@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 15:01:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 39/49] x86 peephole: %rbp-slot reasoning only under a proven
 frame pointer; tail calls keep %rdx

lccc omits the frame pointer, so `disp(%rbp)` is a frame slot only in a
function that establishes one; elsewhere it dereferences a data register.
The StoreRbp/LoadRbp classification is frame-blind. Audit of every
consumer that reasons about the slot rather than the register:

  sound, already guarded: store_forwarding and dead_code (all three
  store-deleting paths; per-function `movq %rsp, %rbp` tracking),
  spill_deref (explicit frame check), frame_compact and callee_saves
  (fire only after `pushq %rbp; movq %rsp, %rbp`; so do all callers of
  helpers::is_near_epilogue), compare_branch (its boolean-slot store
  deletion is licensed by FpLiveness, which makes a frameless function
  with any `(%rbp)` access opaque, so the query fails closed),
  load_op_fuse (37e275359), memory_fold (folds only into the adjacent
  instruction or across register copies, so no memory write
  intervenes);
  slot identity unused: push_pop, self_zext, ebb_reuse, helpers'
  register queries, loop_trampoline (records stack loads only to keep
  the trampoline; never coalesces them).

Two were not sound:

* tail_call: the loads between the call and `ret` move before the jump.
  Only %rax was refused, so an %rdx reload -- the second half of a
  16-byte return -- would be replaced by the callee's %rdx; and in a
  frameless epilogue (`addq $N, %rsp`) a `disp(%rbp)` load is a pointer
  dereference that the move hoists above the callee's stores, or above a
  callee that never returns onto an address the original never touched.
  Now %rdx destinations refuse, and %rbp-based loads are accepted only
  when the epilogue tears down an %rbp frame (`movq %rbp, %rsp`).
* eliminate_dead_sign_extensions, full-width-store path: deletes `cltq`
  before `movq %rax, disp(%rbp)` when the slot is only read narrowly
  afterwards -- slot reasoning. Without a frame the store writes an object
  whose upper half later code or the caller may read. Now it requires
  `rbp_is_frame_pointer` (shared from load_op_fuse) for a %rbp base.

Neither is reachable from lccc's current output: no -O0..-Os build of 16-
byte-returning forwarders converts (the stack-window gate blocks them),
and v8 -> v9 assembly is byte-identical over the 1,220-file regression
corpus at -O2 and -O0 and the 86 benchmark programs at every level. The
guards make the predicates true on their own instead of resting on an
unrelated gate.

Tests pair each refusal with an accepting control differing in one
detail: %rdx vs %rcx (also end to end through peephole_optimize, with the
function's LCCC_RET_RDX contract), `8(%rbp)` vs `8(%rsp)` in a frameless
epilogue, frame prologue present vs absent for the cltq path.
