From: ms178 <m.seyfarth@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 18:55:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 40/49] liveness: an empty asm template does not make register
 operands inert

PR #1039 treated every empty-template asm as a non-call point, but the emitter
still stages its register operands through caller-saved registers, so a value
live across it in %rcx/%rdx was clobbered (wrong result vs gcc-16 at x86-64
O1..Os). inline_asm_is_register_inert() is the one predicate liveness and the
emitter share: no goto labels, empty template, every operand memory-only
(m/o/V) or immediate. x86-64 -O2 corpus asm unchanged.
