From 167d519b0e7a3154827f88fbf19699b3b8056f08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ms178 <m.seyfarth@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 18:55:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 41/49] i686: direct-home copies, slot RMW across CFG,
 section-aware extents, add/sub $1 when CF is dead

* copy_into_home: the direct-home copy no longer reads a home it overwrote.
* collapse_slot_rmw_i686: local scan first; the CFG liveness oracle only after
  a barrier or end of function.
* function_extents: section-aware (data labels inside .rodata no longer end a
  function's extent; jump-table islands stay inside it).
* incl/decl on memory -> addl/subl $1 only when CF is provably dead
  (uops.info: INC M32 is 3 fused uops on SKL/ADL-P vs 2 for ADD M32,I8).
