From e5ab5ce579ba85228e5da537a4236c7f693dcb9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ms178 <m.seyfarth@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 19:32:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 48/49] i686 peephole: `(%ebp)` is a frame slot only under a
 frame proof

Under -fomit-frame-pointer the allocator hands %ebp out like any other
callee-saved register, but the peephole classified every `N(%ebp)` operand
as a frame slot. In benchmark i32_product_map's init loop (-m32 -O1, main
and this series alike) `&a[i]` and then `&b[i]` were homed in %ebp, and the
windowed dead-store pass deleted `movl %edi, (%ebp)` -- the a[i] store --
because the b[i] store "overwrote the same slot": a[] stayed zero and the
program printed the zero-input hash.

* `LineInfo::ebp_gpr`: the line's function has no frame proof. The proof
  is positive -- the function's own `movl %esp, %ebp` -- and the default is
  the data-register reading, for lines outside every function too.
  Mentioning `(%ebp)` is not a proof; it is what a data %ebp does.
* `classify_all` classifies a text and marks functions; both entry points
  (the peephole and the terminal epilogue merge) use it.
* `classify_line_ctx` and `data_ebp_view` are the one definition: no
  `LineKind` records a memory base register, so a `(%ebp)` operand on a
  data %ebp classifies exactly like the same operand on any other base --
  an indirect access, no slot kind, no frame offset. Every one of the 54
  re-classification sites carries the line's own context, and the textual
  frame-operand parsers (`parse_immediate_store`, `frame_write_extents`
  via `frame_kill_extents`) read the same view.
* Audited the remaining textual `(%ebp)` sites: the narrow compare fold
  moves the load only across no-ops and refuses %ebp as destination; the
  never-read-store pass has its own frame proof for `leal`; the frame and
  tail-call detectors err towards keeping the frame. No change needed.

Tests: classification equivalence against another base register for 14
operand forms in both contexts; `classify_all` grants slots only under a
proof; the miscompile shape (register, immediate and byte stores through a
reloaded data %ebp) survives the whole peephole while the framed control
still loses its dead store. Runtime: ebp_data_register_stores_i686 at
-O1/-O2/-Os, which fails on main (4096 wrong elements).
